# Interior comment inside a SINGLE-ELEMENT tuple — live regression pin.
#
# CELL (Core #12): axis = fill-emitted region kind; this file samples the
# ONE region that deliberately does NOT route through the delimited-list
# chokepoint. `(x,)` is spelled with a trailing comma because the comma IS
# the tuple, so the `elems.len() == 1` branch emits it flat rather than
# fill-packing it — and a flat emission cannot carry a comment. The branch
# therefore evaluates the interior-comment gate ITSELF, the second and only
# other `has_interior_comments` call in the formatter, and hands a
# comment-bearing 1-tuple to the exploded form (whose own trailing comma
# re-parses as a 1-tuple, so nothing is lost).
#
# RED-VERIFIED against the pre-fix binary: `# inner` dedented out of the
# tuple to statement indent and became a leading comment of `print(t.0)` —
#     auto t = (42,)
#     # inner
#     print(t.0)
#
# The paired assertion pins `# inner` at 8-space indent, inside the parens.

int main():
    auto t = (
        # inner
        42,
    )
    print(t.0)
    return 0
